	"web_text": "In the Ashanti Empire (now part of Ghana), an akonkromfi or royal throne, symbolized the authority and power of the monarch. The akonkromfi is carved in wood and decorated with shiny brass knobs and tacks, and carved animals. Their designs are filled with meaning often included adinkra symbols. These symbols, originally from the Akan people, tell stories and represent ideas like wisdom, strength, and peace. This chair is a powerful emblem of the Ashanti king or queen’s power and is used in important ceremonies to emphasize the continuity, dignity, and grandeur of the monarchy.",
